        "source": "NWS Storm Survey",
        "event_narrative": "NWS survey team confirmed an EF-2 tornado in northeastern Newberry County. The tornado touched down near or just before the intersection of Old Blair Road and Henderson Ferry Road where it snapped branches of multiple pine trees and uprooted or snapped several other pines. The tornado crossed the clearing and followed Old Blair Road_ snapping and uprooting various hardwood and softwood trees. A home located off of Old Blair Road had several large pine trees snapped or uprooted around the property. There was a small camper on the property which was flipped. As the tornado continued northeastward towards the Broad River it reached the maximum intensity with peak winds estimated to be 115 mph. Much of the forested area along Old Blair Road was destroyed with numerous snapped pine trees found along and north of the road. The trees also brought down several power poles after falling on the poles or attached lines. The tornado lifted just before reaching the Broad River."
